@startuml seq-planning-agent
' Origin: drafted with AI assistance (Claude Code) from PlanningTools, GeminiPlanningAgent and the real tool log of 2026-10-19; reviewed by the author.
title Planning agent: tool-use loop with guardrails in code (FR-04)
actor Student
participant "StudyPlanController\n/ StudyPlanService" as Svc
participant "GeminiPlanningAgent\n(LangChain4j AiServices)" as Agent
participant "Gemini LLM" as LLM
participant "PlanningTools" as Tools
participant "StudyPlan\n(aggregate)" as Plan
participant "focus-service\nGET /progress" as Focus

Student -> Svc : POST /plans {weekStart, replace}
Svc -> Svc : checks before any LLM call:\nMonday? week not over? slots + topics? (400)\nplan exists and replace≠true? (409)
Svc -> Agent : plan(StudyPlan, courses, availability)
Agent -> LLM : system instructions + "plan my week"
loop the LLM decides which tool to call next
  LLM -> Tools : getDeadlines / getAvailability / getTopics (ranked by TopicPriority)
  LLM -> Tools : getFocusStats
  Tools -> Focus : RestClient GET /progress/{userId}
  LLM -> Tools : addBlocks([...])
  Tools -> Plan : addBlock() per block
  Plan --> Tools : ok, or DomainException\n(outside slot, <25 / >90 min, <10 min gap, past)
  Tools --> LLM : "Added n block(s)" + "REFUSED block k: reason"
  LLM -> Tools : reportInsufficientTime(reason)
  Tools -> Plan : refused while the plan is empty\nand a later slot is still free
end
LLM --> Agent : final reply = plan summary
Agent --> Svc : summary
Svc --> Student : 201 plan with blocks, rationale, shortfall
note over Svc, LLM : LLM error (quota, network, no key) → 503, nothing saved
@enduml
